change runs one `","files":[],"additions":2050,"deletions":3748,"changed_files":72,"merge_commit":"1a691ac6a222b95c46859c9c06d162d6442950a4"},{"number":1293,"title":"Remove obsolete directions and orphaned .lf memory","body":"Remove the retired `.lf/directions/` directory and orphaned `.lf/name-attribution.md`. Curate useful continuation, attribution, ","files":[],"additions":148,"deletions":407,"changed_files":5,"merge_commit":"52dbd45589420995b4202e84f8761a91032d44ce"},{"number":1294,"title":"release: v0.12.22","body":"# v0.12.22\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.22 keeps work moving through review, revision, and delive","files":[],"additions":110,"deletions":42,"changed_files":10,"merge_commit":"8ae6c6421978e0b013ec9abe34189f8dcfa651e2"},{"number":1295,"title":"Resume sessions without injecting prompts and use Git names by default","body":"Reopening or moving a session now resumes the existing conversation without injecting a participant-update prompt. A missing Loo","files":[],"additions":191,"deletions":101,"changed_files":16,"merge_commit":"a48eeb6aed383123c51a6c6cc673591ae19b1417"},{"number":1296,"title":"Resume conversations and Flows from durable Session records","body":"Conversation identity, command outcomes, and Flow progress were scattered across files and overlapping records, making recovery ","files":[],"additions":43237,"deletions":24821,"changed_files":320,"merge_commit":"d296b4805720d1024b53239a85d960fae097963f"},{"number":1297,"title":"Clarify Loopflow’s first steps and use an installed coding agent","body":"Newcomers had to decode Loopflow’s terminology before understanding how to start, and unconfigured runs assumed Codex was inst","files":[],"additions":965,"deletions":228,"changed_files":26,"merge_commit":"102522bc25adc146d4b8cc3f343677ed8170f636"},{"number":1298,"title":"release: v0.12.22","body":"# v0.12.22\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.22 keeps a Task's plan, conversation, review feedback, an","files":[],"additions":66,"deletions":32,"changed_files":2,"merge_commit":"fe74e571607e33111ad660ab52c94f03ccaaeae7"},{"number":1300,"title":"Navigate work with ⌘K and Task links, and inspect folded Flow templates","body":"Finding work in Desktop required navigating the sidebar, and Flow previews exposed every composed step at once. This PR adds sea","files":[],"additions":2441,"deletions":83,"changed_files":26,"merge_commit":"de074a2ebd2cb54e6f7dde799400dae36c87bbbe"},{"number":1301,"title":"Keep Task agent choices and make stalled work visible","body":"Unattended Tasks could ignore `-m` and leave failed decisions looking ready. This change persists the Task's agent choice, expos","files":[],"additions":3105,"deletions":964,"changed_files":75,"merge_commit":"90a232aaff12d9a2fa21fc9fe43a5c6a20074ddf"},{"number":1302,"title":"Delete Linear Tasks through lf and consolidate planning commands","body":"Removing a Task previously required separate Linear and local actions, while planning commands were split across `task`, `pm`, a","files":[],"additions":7242,"deletions":3054,"changed_files":113,"merge_commit":"513966f4ad7c258dcdf6f8a3b0d3fb9eecd49f24"},{"number":1305,"title":"Let a release retry its version after a withdrawn PR, and bound the Swift test step","body":"Two fixes that were blocking the v0.12.23 release on 2026-09-27.\n\n**`lf release run` starts fresh after a withdrawn release PR.*","files":[],"additions":36,"deletions":11,"changed_files":2,"merge_commit":"841164083e87779158b572ccc908a8d4f0dfab6a"},{"number":1306,"title":"release: v0.12.23","body":"# v0.12.23\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.23 makes unattended Tasks easier to steer and recover: ag","files":[],"additions":141,"deletions":137,"changed_files":11,"merge_commit":"5bdcef6b65419d5db2583ee791cede2f1a95b3df"},{"number":1307,"title":"Unify account auth, remember browser profiles, and retain usage evidence","body":"Account login and inspection were spread across separate commands, Claude's normal hyperlink output could time out before openin","files":[],"additions":4943,"deletions":2022,"changed_files":44,"merge_commit":"280670217b0da8f2a541b655b9965c79124a1660"},{"number":1308,"title":"Keep branch builds on private data and installed Tasks on their owning runtime","body":"Running a branch build could expose installed Task history to development migrations and inherited execution context. Branch bui","files":[],"additions":4272,"deletions":2910,"changed_files":167,"merge_commit":"418e52ba652c4054879da67851f18d23e6b64a62"},{"number":1309,"title":"release: v0.12.24","body":"# v0.12.24\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.24 makes account access, Task execution, and unattended r","files":[],"additions":89,"deletions":30,"changed_files":8,"merge_commit":"3c70148e46e58cf60fb3bd35b1b64391540e4906"},{"number":1310,"title":"Realign plans and code before publishing Task work","body":"Task review bundled reconciliation with PR publication and required reports that could drift from the work. This PR adds `realig","files":[],"additions":986,"deletions":864,"changed_files":68,"merge_commit":"c512813b5b333f2ae012503b1781fcbd458be67a"},{"number":1311,"title":"Recover failed release CI and preserve cron failures","body":"Scheduled releases now hand failed required checks to the existing landing repair supervisor, and cron receives the release oper","files":[],"additions":436,"deletions":36,"changed_files":15,"merge_commit":"632b67ec7e98be40fd0b9720b513165f90ef2bef"},{"number":1312,"title":"Simplify repair and delivery choices and add manual S1–S5 operation","body":"Overlapping skills and Flow shortcuts made it difficult to choose how to repair a failure, advance a change, or operate Waves. T","files":[],"additions":1083,"deletions":2605,"changed_files":87,"merge_commit":"ea03788fa4a5697ebb390a62bf24f54ab4b4928f"},{"number":1316,"title":"Read and edit Task files beside the conversation","body":"Reviewing and editing Task files previously meant leaving the conversation or using the terminal. The Mac app now puts scratch n","files":[],"additions":3100,"deletions":380,"changed_files":38,"merge_commit":"4e3e55658c034f3276f67351356d834b7c06d5a5"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.32\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.32 helps operators recover Tasks stalled by unrelated execution history or a missing GitHub PR link. Recovery preserves the Task’s history, checkout and unfinished work, while PR reconciliation can rediscover an existing delivery and record authoritative merge evidence.\n\n## Recover workers without discarding history\n\nUnrelated historical Execs with missing process receipts no longer prevent Task worker recovery. Evidence of current work still controls whether recovery can proceed.\n\n- Live processes, unresolved current Session drivers and Flow claims still block recovery.\n- Task completion and cleanup retain stricter checks; recovering a worker does not authorize removing unfinished work.\n\n## Restore missing PR links\n\nRun `lf pr reconcile` when a Task has lost its GitHub PR identity. Reconciliation uses the Task’s recorded branch to discover an existing PR and recover its delivery evidence.\n\n- A unique matching PR restores the GitHub identity and, when merged, records authoritative merge evidence.\n- Missing or ambiguous matches and failed provider reads preserve local work and leave delivery unresolved.\n- Ordinary status checks do not search unpublished branches. Reconciliation keeps the Task open and local edits intact.\n\n## Operational notes\n\nThe supplied change records passing reconciliation, Task-work and Session-record coverage, the scorecard regression, formatting and all-target Clippy. Installed worker recovery and continuation, including the missing-link reconciliation walkthrough, still need end-to-end verification.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":33,"merged_prs":89,"commit_files":7553,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":531076,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}